body:
## What Problem This Solves

Fixes PostgreSQL connection credentials being inherited by host exec and sandbox child processes when the Gateway reads its DSN from an environment variable, including custom names.

## User Impact

Gateway database credentials stay out of inherited child environments. Explicit command overrides and operator-configured sandbox environment values remain supported. Changing the credential source requires a process restart. No schema, migration, or database-pool behavior changes.

## Why This Change Was Made

Retain environment-source provenance through SecretRef resolution and whole-value config substitution, register it with the existing Gateway credential owner, and reuse that owner in inherited sandbox filtering. Preserve current PostgreSQL pool prewarming.

Ports only the credential-isolation portion of [Galin Iliev’s source commit](https://github.com/galiniliev/openclaw/commit/2c4173934ae1074ecca1b1f48eb13410c143d603). Credit: @galiniliev.

## Evidence

### Actual final-effect proof — passed October 31, 2026

The earlier [Silver review](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/189532#issuecomment-6546045234) had no code findings; all three attention items requested actual child-launch evidence. The missing boundary has now been exercised, not inferred from sanitizer outputs:

| Real path | Observation |
|---|---|
| Real startGatewayServer through startModelsGateway; authenticated operator client; sessions.patch then sessions.list | Session write/read succeeded. The selected source remained CUSTOM_STORE_CONNECTION; a real PostgreSQL SELECT 1 using the retained selection succeeded. |
| Live admitted caller identity → ordinary createExecTool, host gateway → actual shell child | CUSTOM_STORE_CONNECTION was absent; child exited 0. |
| The same exec tool with the production SSH sandbox backend → real SSH client/server → actual shell child | The inherited source was absent; child exited 0. An unfiltered synthetic SendEnv/AcceptEnv control succeeded first, proving that the transport could forward this variable. |
| Separately supplied replacement env for host exec and sandbox exec | Each actual child verified its intended synthetic replacement and exited 0. |
| Same DSN, alternate env source passed through the canonical resolver and Gateway installer | Replacement was rejected with the restart-required error. Subsequent host and sandbox children still lacked the original source; authenticated Gateway session reads still succeeded. |

No mocked Gateway, exec launcher, SSH transport, PostgreSQL server, or sanitizer-output substitute was used. No inference call was needed: authenticated Gateway RPC and real admitted tool execution exercised the required authority and launch boundaries. SSH used an owned loopback server/workspace; this proves environment propagation, not kernel/container containment.

Runtime: Node 26.12.1; PostgreSQL 17.11/pgvector, pinned image SHA-256 151aa1c2e849e7828ed8aef2183ae15f692cbe887d2f28921d8b44b26e154d7e. PostgreSQL ran rootless, network-disabled, with a private Unix socket, read-only root filesystem, dropped capabilities, and synthetic data. No operator Gateway or user database was accessed. Gateway and SSH servers stopped; the owned database container was removed and the post-run container query was empty.

Source binding: executed runtime files were exactly 71c604de0fb5879bb556f674979a47cef0bd1a1f; the only candidate changes were the memory-test fixture/allocation repair now committed as f2060d55c031ac068bf0fe6f2677622b5a62d0bc. Published head 6b3a46f10e4cd366cef8923bd0d46c06b8b823a6 adds an empty attribution marker only. Both new commits are authored by @roboclaw-bot and carry the exact @galiniliev coauthor trailer. Production source is unchanged between the executed and published trees.

<details>
<summary>Redacted command and observed output</summary>

```sh
OPENCLAW_VITEST_RUNTIME=node node scripts/test-database-conformance.mjs \
  --engine postgres --connection "$DISPOSABLE_DSN" -- \
  src/gateway/server-database-engine.runtime-proof.postgres.test.ts \
  src/infra/database-engine/memory-public.postgres.test.ts --maxWorkers=1
```

```text
PROOF SSH_AUTH_AND_SENDENV_OK
PROOF gateway_authenticated_session_write_read=PASS postgres_retained_access=PASS
PROOF gateway_inherited_absent=PASS
PROOF sandbox_inherited_absent=PASS
PROOF gateway_explicit_replacement=PASS
PROOF sandbox_explicit_replacement=PASS
PROOF gateway_inherited_absent=PASS
PROOF sandbox_inherited_absent=PASS
PROOF rejected_replacement_retains_original_protection=PASS gateway_still_serves_postgres_session=PASS
Gateway proof: 1 test passed; test time 43.991 s; shard wall time 192.09 s.
```

The enclosing combined command exited 1 because of the separate memory-test timeout below. The Gateway proof shard independently passed; no aggregate green is claimed.

</details>

<details>
<summary>Executed production-path harness, synthetic token and endpoint redacted</summary>

This disposable harness was staged at src/gateway/server-database-engine.runtime-proof.postgres.test.ts and removed after execution; it is not an added product test. Original harness SHA-256: 62e69c8210dcc6f70e9f2c15b36efc2ade726159ce52f5486daefd6e666a3287. Fixture-driver SHA-256: 88950912cfeec3688ff4c4bb0ae487cefdcace53393c92013bbaefa95ade0f16. The SSH command wrapper executed the real SSH binary with SendEnv=CUSTOM_STORE_CONNECTION against the owned server configured with AcceptEnv for that variable. The copy below redacts the synthetic token and endpoint; it is not byte-identical to the hashed original.

```ts
// Disposable PR189532 proof harness; not a product test or committed change.
import path from "node:path";
import { getEnvironmentData } from "node:worker_threads";
import pg from "pg";
import { afterAll, expect, it } from "vitest";
import { createOperationalRunInstanceRef, prepareAgentRunAdmission } from "../agents/admitted-run-context.js";
import { createExecTool } from "../agents/bash-tools.exec-run.js";
import { fullGatewayExec } from "../agents/bash-tools.lifecycle.test-support.js";
import type { BashSandboxConfig } from "../agents/bash-tools.shared.js";
import { resolveSandboxConfigForAgent } from "../agents/sandbox/config.js";
import { createPreprovisionedSshSandboxBackend } from "../agents/sandbox/ssh-backend.js";
import { createAdmittedGatewayToolCallerIdentity, withGatewayToolCallerIdentity } from "../agents/tools/gateway-caller-context.js";
import { resolveDatabaseEngineSelection } from "../infra/database-engine/config.js";
import { getDatabaseEngineSelection } from "../infra/database-engine/context.js";
import { resetDatabaseEngineSelectionForTest } from "../infra/database-engine/context.test-support.js";
import { setGatewayCredentialEnvKeys } from "../infra/host-env-security.js";
import { createModelsTestState, modelsTestConfig, startModelsGateway } from "./server-methods/models-integration.test-support.js";
import { installGatewayDatabaseEngine } from "./server-database-engine.js";

const connection = getEnvironmentData("openclaw.test.state.conformance.connection");
const key = "CUSTOM_STORE_CONNECTION";
afterAll(() => {
  setGatewayCredentialEnvKeys("database.postgres.connection", []);
  resetDatabaseEngineSelectionForTest();
});
const quote = (s: string) => "'" + s.replaceAll("'", "'\''") + "'";

it.skipIf(typeof connection !== "string")("PR189532 final effects through real Gateway, host exec and SSH sandbox", async () => {
  if (typeof connection !== "string") throw new Error("PostgreSQL fixture connection required");
  const sshRoot = path.resolve(".openclaw/tmp/p1ssh");
  await using state = await createModelsTestState("pr189532-final-effects", { env: {
    [key]: connection, OPENCLAW_EXEC_SHELL_SNAPSHOT: "0", SHELL: "/bin/sh",
    OPENCLAW_SKIP_PROVIDERS: "1", OPENCLAW_TEST_MINIMAL_GATEWAY: "1",
  } });
  const token = "<synthetic fixture token>";
  const cfg = modelsTestConfig(state, token, {
    database: { engine: "postgres", postgres: { connection: { source: "env", provider: "default", id: key }, schemaPrefix: "pr189532proof" } },
    tools: { exec: fullGatewayExec },
    skills: { load: { watch: false } },
  });
  const gateway = await startModelsGateway(state, cfg, token);
  try {
    const sessionKey = "agent:main:pr189532-proof";
    const result = await gateway.client.request("sessions.patch", { key: sessionKey, label: "PR189532 database credential final-effect proof" });
    expect(result).toBeTruthy();
    const listed = await gateway.client.request("sessions.list", {});
    expect(JSON.stringify(listed)).toContain("pr189532-proof");
    const selected = getDatabaseEngineSelection();
    expect(selected?.postgres?.connectionEnvKey).toBe(key);
    expect(process.env[key] === connection).toBe(true);
    const db = new pg.Client({ connectionString: selected?.postgres?.connection });
    await db.connect();
    try { expect((await db.query("SELECT 1 AS retained")).rows[0].retained).toBe(1); }
    finally { await db.end(); }
    console.log("PROOF gateway_authenticated_session_write_read=PASS postgres_retained_access=PASS");

    const sandboxCfg = resolveSandboxConfigForAgent({ agents: { defaults: { sandbox: {
      mode: "all", backend: "ssh", scope: "session", workspaceAccess: "rw",
      ssh: { target: "fixture-user@<loopback>:<owned-ssh-port>", command: path.join(sshRoot, "ssh-sendenv"), identityFile: path.join(sshRoot, "client"), strictHostKeyChecking: false, updateHostKeys: false, workspaceRoot: state.workspaceDir },
    } } } }, "main");
    const backend = await createPreprovisionedSshSandboxBackend({
      sessionKey, scopeKey: sessionKey, workspaceDir: state.workspaceDir, agentWorkspaceDir: state.workspaceDir, cfg: sandboxCfg,
    }, { runtimeId: "pr189532-proof-ssh", remoteWorkspaceDir: state.workspaceDir });
    const sandbox: BashSandboxConfig = {
      containerName: backend.runtimeId, workspaceDir: state.workspaceDir, containerWorkdir: backend.workdir,
      workdirValidation: backend.workdirValidation, validateWorkdir: backend.validateWorkdir,
      discardPreparedWorkdir: backend.discardPreparedWorkdir, workdirRoots: backend.workdirRoots,
      buildExecSpec: backend.buildExecSpec, finalizeExec: backend.finalizeExec,
    };
    let sequence = 0;
    const probe = async (target: "gateway" | "sandbox", replacement?: string) => {
      const runId = "pr189532-proof-" + (++sequence);
      const admission = prepareAgentRunAdmission({ cfg, operationalRunInstance: createOperationalRunInstanceRef(runId), facts: {
        runId, agentId: "main", ingress: { kind: "schedule", boundary: "cron.script", state: "present" },
      } });
      try {
        const admitted = await admission.admit("gateway");
        const caller = createAdmittedGatewayToolCallerIdentity({ admittedRunContext: admitted, agentId: "main", sessionKey });
        if (!caller) throw new Error("No admitted Gateway caller");
        const tool = createExecTool({ config: cfg, agentId: "main", sessionKey, scopeKey: sessionKey, runId,
          operationalRunInstance: admitted.operationalRunInstance, trigger: "cron", ...fullGatewayExec,
          host: target, ...(target === "sandbox" ? { sandbox } : {}), cwd: state.workspaceDir, notifyOnExit: false, allowBackground: false,
        });
        const command = replacement
          ? 'test "$CUSTOM_STORE_CONNECTION" = ' + quote(replacement) + ' && printf REPLACEMENT_REACHED'
          : 'test "${CUSTOM_STORE_CONNECTION+x}" != x && printf INHERITED_ABSENT';
        const output = await withGatewayToolCallerIdentity(caller, () => tool.execute(runId, {
          command, ...(replacement ? { env: { [key]: replacement } } : {}), timeoutSeconds: 30, yieldMs: 10000,
        }));
        expect(output.details).toMatchObject({ status: "completed", exitCode: 0 });
        expect(JSON.stringify(output)).toContain(replacement ? "REPLACEMENT_REACHED" : "INHERITED_ABSENT");
        console.log("PROOF " + target + "_" + (replacement ? "explicit_replacement" : "inherited_absent") + "=PASS");
      } finally { admission.close(); }
    };
    await probe("gateway");
    await probe("sandbox");
    await probe("gateway", "synthetic-host-replacement");
    await probe("sandbox", "synthetic-sandbox-replacement");
    const next = await resolveDatabaseEngineSelection({ ...cfg, database: { ...cfg.database, postgres: {
      ...cfg.database?.postgres, connection: { source: "env", provider: "default", id: "REJECTED_STORE_CONNECTION" },
    } } }, { REJECTED_STORE_CONNECTION: connection });
    await expect(installGatewayDatabaseEngine(undefined, next)).rejects.toThrow("restart the process");
    expect(getDatabaseEngineSelection()?.postgres?.connectionEnvKey).toBe(key);
    await probe("gateway");
    await probe("sandbox");
    expect(JSON.stringify(await gateway.client.request("sessions.list", {}))).toContain("pr189532-proof");
    console.log("PROOF rejected_replacement_retains_original_protection=PASS gateway_still_serves_postgres_session=PASS");
  } finally {
    await gateway.close();
  }
}, 600_000);

```

</details>

### CI fixture repair and remaining timing uncertainty

- [Earlier PostgreSQL conformance 3/3](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/41218064742/job/124587005235) executed merge 5032076a43a61423f0a462f2111f3255a1a9a187 (head 71c604de into base cb06c051). Its infra shard had 292 passing tests and one real CLI forget/re-admission failure. The fixture manually installed a selection without connectionEnvKey, then the CLI resolved its env SecretRef canonically. Commit f2060d55 replaces that competing construction with the existing resolver and awaits both callers. Production identity checks and all assertions are unchanged.
- Local cold full-file runs at the existing 120-second test deadline timed out: first 1 failed/3 passed, then 2 failed/2 passed. These failures remain recorded and unresolved. No longer committed timeout, retry, skip, weaker assertion, or broader mock was introduced. Earlier preparation-only attempts also exceeded host budgets and are not product verdicts.
- A bounded diagnosis at the unchanged 120-second deadline, with temporary phase logging and the first case selected, passed the entire public flow in 4.080 s: manager ready 0.851 s, sync 2.534 s, diagnostic verified 3.203 s, forget 3.971 s, reset 4.062 s, re-admission 4.069 s. Three sibling cases were intentionally not selected. This supports the fixture repair but does not establish a fix for the cold-run timeout. Instrumentation was removed; the candidate file SHA-256 was restored exactly to c5aec2e8a6171542f35073bb9a87356e2788c8187e5c8e8a927ee1104aeca4de. Exact-head CI must supply the normal broad verdict.
- Fresh independent local autoreview of the two-file repair, P0–P2 against 71c604de: scoped-clean, no actionable findings, correctness confidence 0.9. It explicitly retains the timeout uncertainty. Infra test typecheck, targeted type-aware lint, formatting, scoped diff checks, and staged test-line ratchet passed. Lint took 51.51 s after boundary-artifact preparation. The allocation shrank from 111 to 110 for the one-line net test reduction; shared scalar unchanged.

### Reused unchanged proof

- Baseline f1c93577085244aa96aa87b53a2df9b59d293bd7: focused regressions reproduced inherited host/sandbox leaks and accepted source replacement (4 failures). The wrapper later detected source drift during cleanup because editing began after assertions; this is not claimed as a clean wrapper run.
- The original fix passed 47 focused tests for credential installation, pool prewarming, config/context and sanitizers. New credential cases took about 2.41 s; changed config cases about 0.21 s. Original Gateway/infra shard wall times were 328.25 s/93.85 s. Core production and Gateway/infra test typechecks, targeted lint, formatting, docs links (16,194; none broken), allocation and whitespace gates passed.
- Original independent P0–P2 autoreview was scoped-clean. It did not certify the unchanged configured-secret resolver internally or full transport; the new runtime proof addresses the missing final-effect boundary without claiming an audit of unrelated resolver internals.
- Simplification: one existing credential owner, no parallel policy store. Production remains +17/-2 lines. Net regression growth is now 110 lines, covered by this PR’s unique allocation.

Current-head CI passed, including all three PostgreSQL conformance shards and the required openclaw/ci-gate ([run 41230568054](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/41230568054)). ClawSweeper awarded [Platinum Hermit (4/6) for readiness, proof, and patch quality](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/189532#issuecomment-6546045234) on head 6b3a46f10e4cd366cef8923bd0d46c06b8b823a6, with no actionable findings. The historical local cold-run timeout uncertainty above remains disclosed; the green CI is not presented as a local timeout fix.

## Worked on by

- @galiniliev

