</details>

- **Exact-head CI:** `ef4f16f4c253f84d951d79bc26d3904bd034bb49` passed all three PostgreSQL conformance shards and the [aggregate CI gate](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/41263453372/job/124726369419). No code or head change was made for this new proof. Current main `72cab24990b3746574ac83e3d73c79530b8cc198` retains byte-identical pre-fix restore-owner source.

Simplification: production **+2 net lines**, regression **+12**; one allocation decision stays with its existing owner. Existing conservative retention of earlier recovery preparations is unchanged.

### Retained native proof receipts — partial recovery

Recovered historical receipts for published head `ef4f16f4c253f84d951d79bc26d3904bd034bb49`. These are retained working-tree/native migration-protocol records, **not** a new run, source push, or managed package-swap qualification.

The tested restore-owner SHA-256 recorded in the retained identity output is `7e92a49f9e88e1b9621fc37a1af868b73fc5a9ccdca157b5f8b9f749ee66f96a`; a fresh read of that file at the published head matched it. This binds the production component, not every historical executable/build input.

**Completeness limits:** the complete retained 2026.10.9 completion output and source/package identity read are below. The original RED/GREEN stdout records available through retained history are only 8,000-character prefixes; their safe phase/code projections and native driver completion metadata are included, but missing tails are not inferred. Original raw log files, complete build-input-signature files, and detailed custody/lifecycle artifacts could not be reread. **This partial recovery does not fully close the raw-artifact/custody request.** The `released` field is preserved verbatim and must not be treated as a process/lease-release assertion.

<details>
<summary>Exact retained 2026.10.9 terminal output — driver exit 0, 178,487 ms</summary>

Receipt bytes: 2,914; SHA-256 `cde37968e9b10c39357114ccba95d721d8ff4ccedbf37979c5cd7425690f7967`.

