## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: slow or unavailable remote worker recovery can keep the Gateway from becoming ready after restart.

## User Impact

The Gateway can become ready while remote workers reconcile. Local workspace journals still settle first, and shutdown waits for tracked recovery before closing environments. Remote recovery errors remain reported through the existing owner.

## Why This Change Was Made

Schedule provider reconciliation through the existing tracked recovery chain instead of awaiting it on the readiness path. Reuse the native placement lifecycle and shutdown drain; restart recovery only owns the exact interrupted claims captured before new admission.

