## What Problem This Solves

Gateway operators cannot choose when automatic update campaigns start.

## User Impact

User impact: Settings → Updates offers hourly (the existing default), daily with a time, weekly with a day/time, and a custom cron expression. Times follow the Gateway host's timezone, which is shown in the UI. The schedule is a campaign-start window, not an exact completion deadline.

## Why This Change Was Made

One optional `update.auto.schedule` cron string stores the policy; presets are UI projections and hourly clears the optional field. Existing configs retain their previous behavior. The existing cron calculator and Gateway scheduler remain the owners; the existing croner dependency is reused and the materialized-wrapper import inventory is updated. No new timezone option or storage migration is introduced by this feature.

Configured windows constrain startup, restart, scheduled checks, and interactive refresh. Hot changes rearm the existing scheduler and retire pending campaigns. Rollout delays, idle/countdown behavior, restart safety, explicit update-now, and the one-hour hold retain their established semantics.

Requested by and implemented for @jacobtomlinson.

