### Prior-head real packaged Gateway scheduling proof

A separate full Gateway ran the installed candidate, with a named synthetic profile and UTC host timezone. The test used the maintained persistent Gateway client and normal operator-token RPCs, not a mocked Gateway or clock. It passed in **197.96 s**:

- Existing configuration with no schedule key loaded successfully.
- A real higher npm beta version (`2026.11.5-beta.1`) was available, but a saved future daily schedule prevented campaign admission on startup and explicit refresh.
- A cold process restart preserved the schedule and unrelated settings/workspace data and still did not start a campaign outside the window.
- Hot-changing to `* * * * *` admitted a countdown at the next matching minute without an interactive refresh.
- Disabling automatic updates through live config canceled the campaign before installation. The saved optional setting and unrelated data remained intact. All owned processes were joined.

The hourly cadence and cron/DST calculations are also covered by the production-owner regression tests; this acceptance run did not wait an entire hour.

